<title>USA: Morgan Stanley's Wien ups stocks in model.</title>
<headline>Morgan Stanley's Wien ups stocks in model.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Stanley Stanley said the firm's U.S. portfolio strategist Byron Wein raised the weighting of stocks in the his model portfolio to 93 percent from 90 percent, dropping cash to seven pct from 10 pct.</p>
<p>Wein added Motorola Inc, Advanced Micro Devices Inc and Kmart Corp to the model portfolio, the firm said.</p>
<p>Advanced Micro was also put on Wein's &quot;fresh money&quot; buy list, Morgan said. United Technologies Corp was removed from the list.</p>
<p>((--Wall St Desk, 212-859-1721))</p>
</text>
